@bank all
// Pillar 5 (head writer, seat W): the Thursday inspection (M3, 24c). Said by the duty officer at your berth (Calder on
// your first, then an officer by rota). Kinds by result: inspect.nod (all three right), inspect.uniform / .bed / .locker
// (only that one wrong), inspect.two (two wrong), inspect.none (all three wrong). Never a fail. Card lines.
// inspect.mail.<result>: the same remark by Mail at 07:00 if you weren't there (TEXT, no voice tokens).

== inspect.nod
- Good. Carry on.
- All in order. Thank you.
- Corners and all. Well done.
== inspect.uniform
- Uniform's seen better days, cadet.
- Bed's good. Locker's good. The uniform isn't.
== inspect.bed
- Make the bed before you go, please.
- The bed looks slept in. It was. Make it anyway.
== inspect.locker
- Locker. Things go in it, not on it.
- Tidy the locker, please. You'll thank yourself.
== inspect.two
- Two out of three. Let's get to three next week.
- Not quite there. Uniform, bed, locker: all three.
== inspect.none
- Uniform, bed and locker. All three. Next Thursday, please.
- We'll call this a practice. Next week counts.

== inspect.mail.nod
- Your berth was in good order this morning. Nothing to add.
== inspect.mail.uniform
- Your berth was tidy. Next time, a clean uniform, please.
== inspect.mail.bed
- Your locker and uniform were fine. Next time, make the bed, please.
== inspect.mail.locker
- Uniform and bed were fine. Next time, a tidy locker, please.
== inspect.mail.two
- Two of the three weren't right this morning. Uniform, bed, locker: all three next week.
== inspect.mail.none
- Your berth wasn't ready this morning. Uniform, bed, locker: next Thursday, please.
